## Greeting Function

Here's a JavaScript function that returns a greeting based on the name and time of day:

```javascript
/**
 * Returns a greeting based on the name and time of day.
 * @param {string} name - The name of the person to greet.
 * @param {number} hour - The hour of the day (0-23).
 * @returns {string} A greeting message.
 */
function getGreeting(name, hour) {
  if (typeof name !== "string" || name.trim() === "") {
    throw new Error("Name must be a non-empty string.");
  }

  if (typeof hour !== "number" || hour < 0 || hour > 23) {
    throw new Error("Hour must be a number between 0 and 23.");
  }

  let timeOfDay;

  if (hour >= 5 && hour < 12) {
    timeOfDay = "morning";
  } else if (hour >= 12 && hour < 17) {
    timeOfDay = "afternoon";
  } else if (hour >= 17 && hour < 21) {
    timeOfDay = "evening";
  } else {
    timeOfDay = "night";
  }

  return `Good ${timeOfDay}, ${name}!`;
}
```

### Example Usage

```javascript
console.log(getGreeting("Alice", 8));   // "Good morning, Alice!"
console.log(getGreeting("Bob", 13));    // "Good afternoon, Bob!"
console.log(getGreeting("Charlie", 18)); // "Good evening, Charlie!"
console.log(getGreeting("Diana", 23));  // "Good night, Diana!"
```

### Using the Current Time

You can also call the function with the current hour automatically:

```javascript
function greetNow(name) {
  const currentHour = new Date().getHours();
  return getGreeting(name, currentHour);
}

console.log(greetNow("Alice")); // Greeting based on the current time
```

### Time of Day Ranges

| Time Range | Greeting |
|---|---|
| 5:00 AM – 11:59 AM | Good morning |
| 12:00 PM – 4:59 PM | Good afternoon |
| 5:00 PM – 8:59 PM | Good evening |
| 9:00 PM – 4:59 AM | Good night |

